GP series: Geometric pregression - its based on ratio -> working over devidenet and multiplications
A geometric progression is a sequence where each term is multiplied by a fixed number called common ration

Components:
a: first term
r: common ratio
n: Number of term
Tn: nth Term
sn: sum of n term

general form of GP : a, ar, ar^2, ar^3  ......

nth term : ar^(n-1)
  ex: 2,6,18,54......
  find the 5th term
  a = 2
  r = 3;
  n = 5
  so, 2*3^(5-1) => 2*3^4 => 2*81 => 162

sum of nth term:
  when r != 1
  sn = a(r^n -1) / r -1    ==========> r > 1
  sn = a(1- r^n) / 1 - r   =========== r < 1
  sn = na =======> r = 1
  Sinf = a/1-r            ============= infinite will come only if r less then 1

  ex: find the first 4 term:
  2,6,18,54
  a = 2;
  r = 3;
  n = 4;
  
  sn = a(r^n -1) / r - 1 => 2(3^4 -1) / 3 - 1 => 2(81 - 1) / 2 => 2(80)/2 => 80

  Infinite GP Sum:
  of r < 1 => then infinite sum exists
  s infinite = a / 1 -r 
  ex: 1 + 1/2 + 1/4 + 1/8 ...
  a = 1;
  r = 1/2;
  s = 1/ 1 - 1/2 => 1/1/2 => 2

